      <memberdef kind="function" id="utility_8h_1a732bb003220387dc7af9c2751c1b2465" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>uint8_t</type>
        <definition>uint8_t crc8</definition>
        <argsstring>(const uint8_t *data, int len)</argsstring>
        <name>crc8</name>
        <param>
          <type>const uint8_t *</type>
          <declname>data</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>len</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Calculates CRC-8 checksum for the given data using SHT40&apos;s polynomial. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This function computes an 8-bit CRC checksum using the polynomial defined in the SHT40 datasheet. It is used to verify data integrity when reading from the SHT40 sensor.</para>
<para>The CRC-8 parameters are:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Initialization value: 0xFF</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Polynomial: 0x31 (x⁸ + x⁵ + x⁴ + 1)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>No final XOR (0x00)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Example from datasheet: For data bytes {0xBE, 0xEF}, the CRC result is 0x92.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the input data buffer. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">len</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Length of the data buffer in bytes.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="attention"><para>Ensure that <computeroutput>data</computeroutput> points to a valid memory location of at least <computeroutput>len</computeroutput> bytes. This function does not perform bounds checking.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>CRC-8 checksum as an 8-bit unsigned integer. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
